'''Mohit Burman''' is an Indian businessman. He is the chairman of [[Dabur]], an Ayurvedic and FMCG company.<ref name="Business Standard">{{cite news |date=13 August 2022 |title=Amit Burman resigns as Dabur chairman, Mohit Burman takes charge |newspaper=Business Standard |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/companies/amit-burman-resigns-as-dabur-chairman-mohit-burman-takes-charge-122081300029_1.html |access-date=1 November 2023}}</ref> A fifth-generation scion of the [[Bengali Hindu]] Burman family, he also led the family's acquisition of a majority stake in dry cell battery maker [[Eveready Industries India]]<ref name="Dabur India Ltd. Official Website">{{cite web |date=20 June 2022 |title=Eveready Industries to augment product portfolio: Mohit Burman of Dabur India |url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/eveready-industries-to-augment-product-portfolio/article65545241.ece |access-date=1 November 2023 |website=The Hindu Business Line |publisher=Dabur India Ltd.}}</ref> and the family's entry into the life insurance sector through [[Aviva India]]. A sports enthusiast, he is also promoter and co-owner of the [[Indian Premier League]] cricket team [[Punjab Kings]].<ref name="mohitbio">{{cite news|title=Preity Zinta, Ness Wadia, Karan Paul, Mohit Burman|date=2 April 2008|url=http://ipl.timesofindia.indiatimes.com/Teams--Profiles/Owners/Preity-Zinta-Ness-Wadia-Karan-Paul-Mohit-Burman/articleshow/2919438.cms|newspaper=[[The Times of India]]|access-date=18 February 2015|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20090523205516/http://ipl.timesofindia.indiatimes.com/Teams--Profiles/Owners/Preity-Zinta-Ness-Wadia-Karan-Paul-Mohit-Burman/articleshow/2919438.cms |archivedate=23 May 2009}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Promoters of Kings XI Punjab|url=http://www.kxip.in/page/promoters|publisher=[[Kings XI Punjab]]|access-date=18 February 2015|archive-date=3 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160303192124/http://www.kxip.in/page/promoters|url-status=dead}}</ref>

==Early life and education==
After completing his schooling from [[Highgate School]], London, he graduated from [[Richmond, The American International University in London|Richmond College]], in Bachelor of Arts, Business Administration and Economics (Double major: Marketing and General Management) and subsequently completed his Master of Business Administration degree, in Finance from [[Babson College|Babson Graduate School of Business, Massachusetts]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Mohit Burman Director of Dabur India Ltd. MBA from Babson Graduate School of Business|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/research/stocks/people/person.asp?personId=28442143&ticker=DABUR:IN|publisher=Bloomberg L.P.|access-date=18 February 2015}}</ref><ref name="mohitburmanbio">{{cite web|title=Mohit Burman Bio |url=http://www.in.com/mohit-burman/biography-393419.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150122200325/http://www.in.com/mohit-burman/biography-393419.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=22 January 2015|website=in.com|access-date=18 February 2015}}</ref>

In October 2024, the Burman family was ranked 23rd on Forbes list of India’s 100 richest tycoons, with a net worth of $10.4 billion.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 9, 2024 |title=India's 100 Richest |url=https://www.forbes.com/lists/india-billionaires/ |website=India’s 100 Richest}}</ref>

==Career==
Burman started his career with Welbeck Property Partnership London and then joined Dabur Finance Ltd., a company specializing in fund and fee-based financial activities, as Senior Manager. He worked in the group's financial services businesses including [[asset management]], [[life insurance]] and pensions by setting up an insurance company with the UK's largest insurance company, [[Aviva]].<ref name="Daburbusiness">{{cite news|title=Dabur Group's Burmans, Espírito Santo Investment Bank Form JV |date=15 November 2011|url=http://www.vccircle.com/news/banking/2011/11/15/dabur-group%C2%92s-burmans-esp%C3%ADrito-santo-investment-bank-form-jv|publisher=Vccircle.com|access-date=18 February 2015}}</ref> His family in November 2011<ref name="NDTV">{{cite news|title=Dabur promoters, Espirito Santo Investment Bank form JV |date=15 February 2011|url=http://profit.ndtv.com/news/market/article-dabur-promoters-espirito-santo-investment-bank-form-jv-153984|publisher=NDTV|access-date=18 February 2015}}</ref> had established a joint venture with [[Espírito Santo Investment Bank]] to set up an [[investment banking]] company in [[India]].{{Citation needed|date=December 2018}}

Burman has also been actively involved in expanding Dabur India's presence in overseas markets, and was involved in the acquisition of Balsara Hygiene and Home Care businesses for Rs. 1.43&nbsp;billion by Dabur India Ltd. on 27 January 2005.<ref name=NDTV />

==Board memberships==
Mohit also holds board membership<ref>{{cite web|title=Board Membership of Mohit Burman|url=http://www.dabur.com/About%20Dabur-Mr.%20Mohit%20Burman|publisher=[[Dabur]]|access-date=18 February 2015}}</ref><ref name="Rediff">{{cite news|title=Dabur's Burmans to enter i-banking, broking | date= 12 October 2011|url=http://www.rediff.com/money/report/daburs-burmans-to-enter-i-banking-broking/20111012.htm|work=[[Rediff.com]]|access-date=18 February 2015}}</ref> of different other companies like [[Federation of Indian Chambers of Commerce]] & Industry, Dabur International Limited, Universal Sompo General Insurance Co. Ltd., KPH Dream Cricket Pvt. Ltd (Kings XI), Aviva Life Insurance Company India Limited,<ref>{{cite web|title=Chairman of Aviva Life Insurance India Ltd.|url=http://www.avivaindia.com/en/AboutUs/BoardofDirectors.aspx|publisher=[[Aviva]]|access-date=18 February 2015}}</ref> Markettopper Securities Pvt. Ltd., Elephant India Advisors Pvt. Ltd., Caterham Cars Pvt. Ltd, H&B Stores Ltd., Espirito Santo Securities India Pvt. Ltd.

==Sports==
Mohit Burman is one of a group of promoters who have formed the [[cricket]] team [[Punjab Kings]].<ref>{{Cite news|agency=PTI|date=2021-02-17|title=IPL franchise Kings XI Punjab renamed Punjab Kings|language=en-IN|work=The Hindu|url=https://www.thehindu.com/sport/cricket/ipl-franchise-kings-xi-punjab-renamed-punjab-kings/article33861159.ece|access-date=2021-05-03|issn=0971-751X}}</ref> He is also a director and co-Owner of a Caribbean Premier League team [[Saint Lucia Kings]].<ref name="Forbes">{{cite magazine |date=17 February 2020 |title=Kings XI Punjab Set To Acquire St Lucia Franchise Of Caribbean Premier League |url=https://www.outlookindia.com/website/story/sports-news-kings-xi-punjab-set-to-acquire-st-lucia-franchise-of-caribbean-premier-league/347469 |magazine=OutlookIndia.com |access-date=1 November 2023}}</ref><ref name="getreading.co.uk">{{cite news |date=17 February 2020 |title=St Lucia Zouks sold to Kings XI Punjab owners |work=ESPN Cric Info |publisher=ESPNcricinfo |url=https://www.espncricinfo.com/story/st-lucia-zouks-sold-to-kings-xi-punjab-owners-1216718 |access-date=1 November 2023}}</ref>

